# netsurf: display: inline-grid is an inline-level box
#
# github.com crashed the simulator (and would crash the Vita: asserts are
# compiled in) at layout_minmax_block_inner's assert(0): a <button> with
# display: inline-grid sat directly in its block. Box construction put an
# inline-grid box straight into the block instead of an inline container:
# every "inline-level atomic box" check named inline-block and inline-flex
# but not inline-grid. Added it wherever inline-flex is handled: box
# construction (7 sites, incl. blockification in a flex container),
# normalisation (as grids are, box_normalise_flex), line layout and min/max
# measurement, and the inline-flow helper.
#
# Two sizing fixes so an inline grid shrinks to fit like a browser's:
# - a grid's intrinsic width is a ROW of its tracks (a px track's size, or
#   its first-row item's width) plus column gaps, not its widest item;
# - layout_grid keeps the shrink-to-fit width layout_float gave an inline
#   or floated grid with width:auto instead of re-resolving it to the line.
# (The redraw clip lines for inline grids are in patch 149.)
# Test: CSS-inline-grid.html 4/4; scorecard github 0 (crash) -> 67.
